# Engine wave E2. "Ada|88".split("|") is [A, d, a, |, 8, 8] on the pinned JDK and was [, A, d, a, |, 8, 8] on the
# fork: a pattern that matches with zero width at the very start of the input made a leading empty piece.
#   - The rule, from the pinned JDK's observed output (runtime/test/cases.mjs, the E2 cases; E2-split-matrix runs
#     String.split and Pattern.split over 11 inputs, 10 patterns and the limits 0, -1, 1, 2 and 3): a match of
#     zero width at index 0 of a non-empty input is no split point. It makes no leading empty piece ("abc".split("")
#     is [a, b, c]; "xax".split("(?=x)") is [xa, x]; "abc".split("\\b", -1) is [abc, ]) and does not count toward
#     a positive limit ("abc".split("", 2) is [a, bc], not [, abc]). A match that takes characters at index 0 is a
#     split point as before (",a".split(",") is [, a]; "abc".split("a*") is [, , b, c]), and so is a zero-width
#     match anywhere else. Pattern.split gave the same as String.split for every input, pattern and limit, and an
#     empty input gave [""] for every pattern and limit, as before.
#   - TPattern.split (which String.split calls) took every match as a split point. Now it skips a match whose end
#     is 0, which is exactly a zero-width match at index 0; nothing else changes. On the fork after this patch,
#     E2-split-matrix prints what the JDK prints, line for line.
#
# Written from TeaVM's own source (classlib/src/main/java/org/teavm/classlib/java/util/regex/TPattern.java) and the
# pinned JDK's observed output; no OpenJDK source was opened (clean room, D14). Written by a subagent (Claude Opus
# 5.5), a language model whose training may include OpenJDK, so the patch was read for names or structure that
# look recalled rather than derived: it adds no name, only one test, in TeaVM's own loop, that the observed rule
# states.
#
# Applies to: github.com/konsoletyper/teavm tag 0.13.1 (b3a245b7). No other patch touches TPattern.

diff --git a/classlib/src/main/java/org/teavm/classlib/java/util/regex/TPattern.java b/classlib/src/main/java/org/teavm/classlib/java/util/regex/TPattern.java
index edd2b34..06f1ae4 100644
--- a/classlib/src/main/java/org/teavm/classlib/java/util/regex/TPattern.java
+++ b/classlib/src/main/java/org/teavm/classlib/java/util/regex/TPattern.java
@@ -187,6 +187,12 @@ public final class TPattern implements Serializable {
             return new String[] { "" }; //$NON-NLS-1$
         } else {
             while (mat.find() && (index + 1 < limit || limit <= 0)) {
+                // teavm-fork: a match of zero width at the very start of the input is no split point, as on the
+                // pinned JDK ("abc".split("") is [a, b, c], with no leading empty piece, while ",a".split(",") is
+                // [, a]); it adds no piece and does not count toward the limit.
+                if (mat.end() == 0) {
+                    continue;
+                }
                 res.add(inputSeq.subSequence(curPos, mat.start()).toString());
                 curPos = mat.end();
                 index++;
